{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/467024-ever-included-someone-famous-in-your-wraith-campaing","id":467024,"title":"Ever included someone 'Famous' in your wraith campaing?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-02T23:12:41-07:00","id":467024,"title":"Ever included someone 'Famous' in your wraith campaing?","content":"mainly that. the ghosts of John Wayne or John Lennon, Jimmy Hendrix or Shackespear, ever used someone famous or Infamous in your game?<br /> <br /> i been thinking about using bonnie and clyde recently...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T23:33:47-07:00","id":467048,"title":"","content":"I never officially stated it, but Julius Caesar is the Smiling Lord of the Grim Legion. The guy has Memoriam up the wazoo.<br /> <br /> I also played my Wraith chronicles in Chicago and used locally known serial killers as major Spectre antagonists; but again never named them outright.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T23:56:53-07:00","id":467076,"title":"","content":"In one Wraith game I was in, the ST used Elvis as a Risen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T08:51:14-07:00","id":467427,"title":"","content":"Alexander the Great as Smiling Lord. Pretty much a Doppleganger/Nephwrack (He has LOTS of Fetters, Memoriam, etc.). His Myrmidon personal guard (also secretly specters) grew increasingly more ant-like as the players encountered them at various points of history. Actually an offstage player in a Mage game. <br /> <br /> Jesse James as a specter, Necropolis: Kansas City game<br /> <br /> Meriwether Lewis, of the Lewis and Clark expedition, as Anacreon of the Silent Legion: St. Louis game. He was crap as his job b/c he kept wandering off to go explore. (His most significant Fetter was William Clark, a vampire and Prince of St. Louis). <br /> <br /> All in St. Louis<br /> Elijah Lewis (borderline famous) a VERY prominent abolitionist. A Heretic against the Hierarchy slave trade. <br /> Pierre LaClede (borderline famous) a French fur trader who was largely responsible for founding St. Louis and Westport (earliest settlement of what later became Kansas City), a Ferryman with a BIG boat, the Relic steamboat &quot;Carillon&quot;<br /> Marie Chouteau (borderline famous), Anacreon of the Silent Legion, effectively the &quot;First Lady&quot; of early St. Louis (contemporary of LaClede's and possibly his lover, despite the business relationship between him and her husband)<br /> <br /> The KC game exists only in hardcopy form at this point and I'm too lazy to go get the files. I'm sure there are more famous people there but they don't leap to mind.<br /> <br /> In both places there are other people who are locally famous, or, at least famous enough to have big monuments that people are curious enough to enter and read the big bronze plaques (also school field trips) to get them Memoriam. <br /> <br /> Some famous people get sucked up in vampire games in both places as well. (Vide William Clark above.) Not all dead people that are hanging around are wraiths, after all. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T00:16:10-07:00","id":506445,"title":"","content":"Yes, I have.. My Chronicle was set in Necropolis: Los Angeles, where the dominant Legions were the Emerald Legion and the Legion of Paupers. The Anacreon for the Paupers was Ambrose Bierce (author of The Devil's Dictionary), and Pancho Villa (who Bierce rode out to join near the end of his life) also served the Beggar Lord as sort of an empowered Regent over the deserts between Los Angeles and San Diego.<br /> <br /> The Emerald Lord's Anacreon was William Mulholland (the brilliant engineer/visionary/thieving shyster whose efforts brought water Los Angeles the water that made its fortune).<br /> <br /> The 1960s bomb-happy terrorist group known as the Symbionese Liberation Army continued to exist as Spook-heavy Renegades.<br /> <br /> Oh, and the Ferryman mentor (every WtO campaign had a Ferryman mentor, right?) known as &quot;the Falcon&quot; was the ghost of Jaques de Molay, the Grandmaster of the Knights Templar who was burned at the stake at the start of the 14th century.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1536-39steps","user":"39Steps","date":". 05-07-2015, 03:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1536-39steps","name":"39Steps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1536_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T07:59:43-07:00","id":506790,"title":"","content":"Knowing my area. Jesse James.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T10:39:06-07:00","id":508191,"title":"","content":"i added Kurt Cobain as the 'King of Bums' on my game, a renegade who lives by his own rules tryingto leave in peace with himself and playing guitar","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T03:06:21-07:00","id":510514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/467024-ever-included-someone-famous-in-your-wraith-campaing?p=508191#post508191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i added Kurt Cobain as the 'King of Bums' on my game, a renegade who lives by his own rules tryingto leave in peace with himself and playing guitar</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, there is a canon Ferryman called &quot;Kurt&quot; who is very, very young, and has a relic motorcycle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5238-herbert_west","name":"Herbert_West","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5238_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"473"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}